  "usage_note": "**Where** joining two clauses to mean *in or to the place that* (*Stay where you are*) is a conjunction, which has its own entry. In informal American speech, **where ... at** is common (*Where are you at?*); in writing, leave out the **at**.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Where you are going?",
      "correct": "Where are you going?",
      "note": "A direct question puts the helping verb before the subject."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "Can you tell me where is the bank?",
      "correct": "Can you tell me where the bank is?",
      "note": "After **tell me**, **know**, and **ask**, the clause after **where** keeps statement order."
    }
